# Bergdb item 001, WP A4: a child with two current parents, then adopted. Node 5
# points to 11 and 13; T(1) gives 13 a pointer to 11 too (TREE fails for 11);
# T(2) deletes 5's pointer to 11, which stays reachable through 13 (A6 fails for
# 11). The records are the model's; the diagnostics do not fail a trace.
TRACE 1
CONFIG adopt
TX 0
NEW 0 9 I
NEW 3 8 I
NEW 5 3 I
NEW 11 1 I
NEW 13 2 I
ADD 0 0 T 3
ADD 3 0 R 5
ADD 5 0 K 10 11
ADD 5 0 K 20 13
REC 0 0 0 field
VER 3 I
H 0 R 5
F 5 0
VER 5 I
H 0 K 10 11
H 0 K 20 13
F 11 0
F 13 0
VER 11 I
VER 13 I
DIRTY
END 0
TX 1
ADD 13 1 K 30 11
REC 1 0 0 field
GD 3 5 13
DIRTY 3 1 5 1 13 1
END 1
TX 2
ADD 5 2 D 1 10
REC 2 0 0 field
GD
DIRTY 3 1 5 1 13 1
END 2
DONE 2
